{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/944799-2e-hack-1e-athanors-in-2e-i-e-z-splat","id":944799,"title":"[2E Hack] 1E Athanors in 2E ( i.e. Z-Splat )","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-06T06:15:14-07:00","id":944799,"title":"[2E Hack] 1E Athanors in 2E ( i.e. Z-Splat )","content":"<b><i>Note:</i></b><i> As always in my Hack topics, if you do not agree with basic idea of it, stop writing in it and move to other parts of forums. We do not need needless flame wars.</i><br /> <br /> One of change in 2E <b>Promethean</b> from 1E is that Athanors are now not Z-Splats that you were preparing for your own New Dawn and life as Redeemed but more \u2018items of memory and Azoth\u2019, leading to repertories off knowledge and some powers for Created. However, I was very found of original concept of Athanors with their \u2018medieval bestiary\u2019 aesthetics - so this topic is about recreating them in 2E games. For ease of communication maybe called them \u2018Bestiary Athanors\u2019?<br /> <br /> Closest to those we have in new corebook are Refinement Furnaces:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PtC 2E, p.94</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Refinement Furnace</b><br /> The Promethean can use a Refinement Furnace to lock part of her alchemical body in attunement to a certain Refinement, whilst the rest of her changes. In essence, she has created an oven within an oven, a feat that she can only accomplish by being a walking alchemical laboratory. The resulting Refinement Furnace allows her to tap into that Refinement\u2019s benefits without spending Vitriol, even when she has left its philosophy behind. This is the only type of Athanor that solely benefits its creator rather than other Prometheans.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Question is this enough for previous Bestiary Athanors \u2013 or new Athanors type is in order to create? </b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T08:42:08-07:00","id":944867,"title":"","content":"A 1e-style Athanor included several aspects:<br /> <br /> \u2022 a pair of Trait Affinities that can be improved using Vitriol.<br /> \u2022 a Promethean Boon that becomes a Redeemed Boon when you reach the New Dawn.<br /> \u2022 a pool of Reagent, a special fuel that can fuel the Promethean Boon, boost supernatural tolerance, suppress Disquiet, resist Torment, hide disfigurement, or mitigate Azothic Radiance. <br /> <br /> I'd take the Reagent Pool and present it as alternate mechanics for the 2e-style Vitriol Fount \u2014 that is, say that a Vitriol Fount produces Reagent based on how much Vitriol you have stored in it, and use 1e's rules for what Reagent can do and how quickly the Fount produces it. The Boons (and the 1e-style Athanor names) would be presented as an extension of the Bestowment system: at Azoth 1, you get a Bestowment; at Azoth 3, you get a Boon (powered by Pyros instead of Reagent). That leaves only the Trait Affinities, which I'd recast as part of the Roles rather than being bundled with the Boons. That is, give each Role a pair of Affinity Traits and say that the Promethean can spend Vitriol to improve them. <br /> <br /> And yes, when you reach the New Dawn, your Boon gets Redeemed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-06-2016, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T00:55:19-07:00","id":945349,"title":"","content":"I think that developers have in making idea of 'let some Alchemy of Created go to the Redeemed'. I just read New Dawn rules and here is what characters got on passing 10 Refinements:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>'PtC 2E, p.187</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character gains ties to the mundane world as though she had completed nine Refinements. If the character remembers everything, she can use an Alembic of one Transmutation that she fixed in her previous life, substituting Willpower for Pyros. If she remembers a mundane existence, the player can spend a further three dots on Social Merits to represent it. The first time she succeeds at a breaking point roll within the following month, she can reverse her choice instead of gaining a Condition \u2014 regaining her memories and supernatural power, or surrendering it for a normal life.</div> </div> </div> </div>All we have to do is just make this new Transmutation possible to be 'locked' for Created without all 10 Refinements - maybe by cost of Willpower dot - and we have nice 1E Athanors variant without writing everything for every 'beast' that was before. Social Merit dots also works good with previous Athanors. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}